WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.020
- I'm a big fan of your work from Glee.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.600
As a part of the LGBTQ community,

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.700
I grew up in a very strict,
religious household,

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.560
maybe something similar
that you can relate to,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.720
and I wanted to ask, as someone

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.010
who never really had a coming out moment,

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.320
what is your advice to the youth of today,

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.180
in America and the world,
that you could give them

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.760
as someone who may be struggling

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.610
with their sexuality or their identity?

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.240
- Well, you said the religious household,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.470
so, you know, to give blanket advice

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.270
to everybody is really hard to do

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.500
because, in some cases, it
might ruin life for the child.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.490
So, it's really one of
those things that there's,

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:39.490
Dan Savage has a program
called It Gets Better

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.620
and I would suggest to anybody

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.090
who's struggling with their sexuality,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.830
who's in a religious family

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.930
or lives in a place where
they wouldn't be accepted

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.280
or if they think they might
even put themselves in danger,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.710
I would go to Dan Savage's It Gets Better.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.180
I mean, President Obama is on it.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.200
It's everybody telling their stories

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.060
about what it was like to come out

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.680
and like, successful people,

00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.840
and some of them are even straight

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.330
who are saying, "Hang in there."

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.210
You'll know when the moment is right

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.950
and it's really hard
for me to tell somebody

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.020
what that moment would be.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.600
You really have to figure
that out for yourself,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.762
but know it gets better, and it does.

00:01:12.762 --> 00:01:15.503
(audience applauds)

